//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// Liquidity Sweep Probability + Targets — Prev Day / Week / Month / Year
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The previous period's HIGH and LOW are where resting stops and pending orders
// pile up. This marks those levels for the Day, Week, Month and Year, puts a
// historically measured probability on each one, and projects a target for the
// move that follows the sweep.
//
//     "The previous day's high has been swept on 63% of days over 4,812 days,
//      and when it was, price reached Target 1 on 41% of them."
//
// PER LEVEL:
//   * SWEEP probability  — how often price traded through that level during the
//                          following period. Wick counts: liquidity taken is
//                          liquidity taken, whether or not it closed beyond.
//   * REVERSAL rate      — of the times it WAS swept, how often price closed
//                          back inside. High reversal = classic stop hunt.
//                          Low reversal = the level breaks and price runs.
//   * RECENT vs ALL-TIME — the same sweep probability over the last N periods
//                          only, so you can see whether behaviour has shifted.
//
// TARGET 1 — two modes:
//
//   CONTINUATION (same side). The sweep keeps going. Target sits on the SAME
//   side as the liquidity that was taken — the next earlier candle that pushed
//   further in that direction:
//
//       previous HIGH swept  ->  T1 = the HIGH of the first earlier candle
//                                whose HIGH is ABOVE the swept candle's high
//       previous LOW  swept  ->  T1 = the LOW of the first earlier candle
//                                whose LOW is BELOW the swept candle's low
//
//   REVERSAL (opposite side). The sweep is a stop hunt and price turns. Target
//   sits on the far side of the swept candle:
//
//       previous HIGH swept  ->  T1 = the LOW of the first earlier candle
//                                whose LOW is BELOW the swept candle's low
//       previous LOW  swept  ->  T1 = the HIGH of the first earlier candle
//                                whose HIGH is ABOVE the swept candle's high
//
//   Both modes start the search two periods back and walk further back until
//   a candle qualifies. Without the "must extend beyond the swept candle"
//   condition the target can land inside the range price has already traded
//   through, which makes it meaningless. If nothing qualifies within the
//   search depth, no target is drawn and that period is excluded from the
//   target statistics rather than counted as a miss.
//
//   Each mode has its own historical hit rate, so running the indicator twice
//   — once per mode — tells you directly whether sweeps on this asset more
//   often continue or reverse.
//
// TARGET 2:
//   The next rung of the same ladder. Where T1 is the first earlier candle
//   that extends beyond the swept one, T2 is the first candle beyond T1 in the
//   same direction — the next pool of liquidity out. Because T2 always sits
//   further away than T1 on the same side, reaching T2 means T1 was passed on
//   the way, so the two hit rates are naturally nested: T2 can never exceed
//   T1. The gap between them is the useful part — it tells you how much of the
//   time a move that gets to T1 keeps going.
//
//   T2 carries its own sample count, because a qualifying second candle does
//   not always exist within the search depth even when the first one does.
//
// WHEN A TARGET IS MISSING:
//   Two reasons, and the table tells them apart. If the T1 column shows a
//   price but no line is on the chart, the level simply has not been swept
//   yet — targets stay hidden until their level is taken unless "Show targets
//   before the sweep" is on. If the column reads "none", no earlier candle
//   within the search depth extends beyond the swept one. That is routine in
//   continuation mode near highs: an upside target needs an EARLIER candle
//   with a higher high, and an asset printing new highs has none nearby.
//   Raise the search depth to reach the previous major high.
//
//   Each target carries its own conditional probability: given the level was
//   swept, how often did price go on to reach that target inside the same
//   period. Targets are drawn only once their level is actually taken (there
//   is an option to show them in advance).
//
// AN HONEST LIMITATION ON THE TARGET STATISTIC:
//   A single higher-timeframe candle records a high and a low but not their
//   order. So the historical figure is strictly "this period swept the level
//   AND traded to the target", which slightly overstates "reached the target
//   AFTER sweeping". Live tracking on your chart does respect the order — a
//   target only counts once its level has already been taken — so the live
//   marker is stricter than the historical percentage beside it.
//
// Highs and lows are measured SEPARATELY, never mirrored — buy-side and
// sell-side liquidity do not get taken at the same rate.
//
// Every line is anchored to the candle that created it, so a level starts at
// its source period and a target starts at whichever earlier period produced
// it. Each carries a price label, and taken levels are marked SWEPT.
//
// DATA: statistics come from the chart symbol's own full higher-timeframe
// history, requested per timeframe. Works on any crypto asset (or anything
// else) with zero configuration. Nothing repaints — every statistic is built
// from confirmed, completed periods only.
//
// NOTE: run this on a chart timeframe FINER than the levels you display. A
// weekly chart cannot resolve daily sweeps.
// =============================================================================

indicator("Liquidity Sweep Probability", shorttitle="LiqSweep",
     overlay=true, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=500, max_boxes_count=500)

// ================================== Inputs ===================================
grpL = "Levels"
onD  = input.bool(true,  "Previous Day    (PDH / PDL)", group=grpL)
onW  = input.bool(true,  "Previous Week   (PWH / PWL)", group=grpL)
onM  = input.bool(true,  "Previous Month  (PMH / PML)", group=grpL)
onY  = input.bool(false, "Previous Year   (PYH / PYL)", group=grpL)
showHi = input.bool(true, "Show highs (buy-side liquidity)", group=grpL)
showLo = input.bool(true, "Show lows (sell-side liquidity)", group=grpL)
hideSwept = input.bool(false, "Hide levels once swept", group=grpL, tooltip="Off by default: a swept level is still information — it tells you the liquidity there is gone.")

grpTg = "Targets"
showTgt   = input.bool(true, "Show Target 1", group=grpTg)
tgtMode   = input.string("Continuation (same side)", "Target direction", options=["Continuation (same side)","Reversal (opposite side)"], group=grpTg, tooltip="Continuation: the sweep keeps running, so the target is the next earlier candle that pushed FURTHER in the same direction — sweep a high, aim for a higher high.\n\nReversal: the sweep is a stop hunt and price turns, so the target is on the far side — sweep a high, aim for a lower low.\n\nEither way the search starts two periods back and keeps walking until it finds a candle that genuinely extends beyond the swept one. Add the indicator twice, once per mode, to see both targets and compare their hit rates.")
showTgt2  = input.bool(true, "Show Target 2", group=grpTg, tooltip="The next rung out: the first candle beyond Target 1 in the same direction. Always further away than T1 on the same side, so its hit rate is always the lower of the two.")
tgtAlways = input.bool(false, "Show targets before the sweep", group=grpTg, tooltip="Off by default, so a target only appears once its level has actually been taken. Turn on to see in advance where each target sits.")
tgtByTf   = input.bool(true, "Colour targets by their timeframe", group=grpTg, tooltip="On: a daily target is drawn in the daily colour, a weekly target in the weekly colour, so every line stays matched to the timeframe it came from. Off: all targets use the single colour below.")
tgtCol    = input.color(#e0e0e0, "Target color (when not coloured by timeframe)", group=grpTg)
tgtLook   = input.int(250, "Target search depth (periods)", minval=3, maxval=1000, group=grpTg, tooltip="How far back to walk looking for a candle that extends beyond the swept one.\n\nThis matters most in continuation mode near highs or lows. An upside target needs an EARLIER candle with a higher high, so when an asset is making new highs — routine on crypto — the nearest one can be hundreds of periods back at the previous major high. A shallow depth finds nothing and no target is drawn.\n\nRaise it if targets are missing; lower it if load time suffers. When nothing qualifies the level is left out of the target statistics rather than counted as a miss.")
tgtSty    = input.string("Dashed", "Target line style", options=["Solid","Dashed","Dotted"], group=grpTg)
tgtW      = input.int(1, "Target line width", minval=1, maxval=4, group=grpTg)

grpS = "Statistics"
recentN = input.int(250, "Recent window (periods)", minval=20, maxval=2000, group=grpS, tooltip="Second sweep probability computed over just the last N completed periods, shown beside the all-time figure. A large gap between them means the behaviour of this level has changed.")
minN    = input.int(30, "Minimum sample to trust", minval=5, maxval=500, group=grpS, tooltip="Below this the probability is shown in amber. The yearly timeframe will sit under it on almost every crypto asset — that is honest, not broken.")
probIn  = input.bool(true, "Show probability in label", group=grpS)

grpC = "Colors"
colD = input.color(#42bda8, "Day",   group=grpC)
colW = input.color(#5b8def, "Week",  group=grpC)
colM = input.color(#c678dd, "Month", group=grpC)
colY = input.color(#e5a54b, "Year",  group=grpC)
sweptCol = input.color(color.new(color.gray, 45), "Swept level", group=grpC)

grpV = "Display"
lineW    = input.int(1, "Line width", minval=1, maxval=4, group=grpV)
lineSty  = input.string("Solid", "Line style", options=["Solid","Dashed","Dotted"], group=grpV)
rightPad = input.int(12, "Extend right (bars)", minval=0, maxval=200, group=grpV)
showBox  = input.bool(false, "Shade the source candle's range", group=grpV, tooltip="Draws a translucent box over the period whose high and low are being marked, so the origin of each pair of lines is unmistakable.")
lblSize  = input.string("small", "Label size", options=["tiny","small","normal"], group=grpV)

grpT = "Stats Table"
showTbl = input.bool(true, "Show table", group=grpT)
tblPos  = input.string("top_right", "Position", options=["top_right","top_left","bottom_right","bottom_left","middle_right"], group=grpT)
tblSize = input.string("small", "Text size", options=["tiny","small","normal","large"], group=grpT)

grpA = "Alerts"
alertOn = input.bool(true, "Fire alert() on sweeps and target hits", group=grpA)

// ============================== Sweep engine =================================
// Runs inside request.security on the level's own timeframe and walks that
// symbol's entire history. Only counters and one small rolling window are
// kept, so this stays light no matter how deep the history goes.
//
// Index map while scoring a completed period:
//   [1] = the period being scored
//   [2] = the period that supplied the level it could sweep (the swept candle)
//   [3] and older = searched for Target 1
// Only completed periods are ever read, so nothing repaints.
//
// Walk back through a rolling buffer of period extremes looking for the first
// candle that reaches beyond `ref`. Returns the price and how many periods
// back it sits, or na when nothing within the buffer qualifies.
f_find(array<float> buf, int startIdx, float ref, bool up) =>
    float res = na
    int off = 0
    int idx = -1
    if startIdx >= 0 and not na(ref)
        int m = array.size(buf)
        for j = startIdx to 0
            float v = array.get(buf, j)
            if up ? v > ref : v < ref
                res := v
                off := m - j
                idx := j
                break
    [res, off, idx]

// Resolve Target 1 for one side of a sweep. `up` falls out of the mode: a high
// sweep continues upward or reverses downward, and a low sweep does the
// reverse, so the side searched is simply whether the sweep and the mode agree.
// Target 2 continues the same walk from just past Target 1, looking for the
// next candle that extends beyond T1 itself. Same buffer, same direction, so
// T2 is always further out than T1.
f_tgts(array<float> hB, array<float> lB, int startIdx, float refHi, float refLo, bool sweptHigh, bool cont) =>
    bool up = sweptHigh == cont
    float v1 = na
    int   o1 = 0
    float v2 = na
    int   o2 = 0
    if up
        [a1, b1, c1] = f_find(hB, startIdx, refHi, true)
        v1 := a1
        o1 := b1
        if not na(a1) and c1 > 0
            [a2, b2, _c2] = f_find(hB, c1 - 1, a1, true)
            v2 := a2
            o2 := b2
    else
        [d1, e1, g1] = f_find(lB, startIdx, refLo, false)
        v1 := d1
        o1 := e1
        if not na(d1) and g1 > 0
            [d2, e2, _g2] = f_find(lB, g1 - 1, d1, false)
            v2 := d2
            o2 := e2
    [v1, o1, v2, o2, up]

f_liq(int recN, int look, bool cont) =>
    var int nTot = 0
    var int swHi = 0
    var int rvHi = 0
    var int swLo = 0
    var int rvLo = 0
    var int swHiT = 0     // sweeps of a high where a target was measurable
    var int swLoT = 0
    var int tgHi  = 0     // ...of those, how many reached Target 1
    var int tgLo  = 0
    var int sw2HiT = 0    // sweeps where a second rung was measurable
    var int sw2LoT = 0
    var int tg2Hi  = 0
    var int tg2Lo  = 0
    var array<float> recHi = array.new<float>()
    var array<float> recLo = array.new<float>()
    // Rolling extremes of completed periods, oldest first, used to search
    // backwards for a valid target.
    var array<float> hBuf = array.new<float>()
    var array<float> lBuf = array.new<float>()

    if bar_index > 1
        float ph = high[2]
        float pl = low[2]
        float h  = high[1]
        float l  = low[1]
        float c  = close[1]
        if not na(ph) and not na(pl) and not na(h) and not na(l)
            nTot += 1
            bool sh = h > ph
            bool sl = l < pl
            if sh
                swHi += 1
                // closed back below the level it took: the sweep failed
                if c < ph
                    rvHi += 1
            if sl
                swLo += 1
                if c > pl
                    rvLo += 1

            // ---- Target 1 ----
            // The buffer has not been extended with this period yet, so its
            // last entry is period [2] — the swept candle — and the search
            // begins one step earlier at [3]. A candidate only qualifies if it
            // reaches beyond the swept candle on the relevant side.
            // Within one candle the order of high and low is unknown, so this
            // measures "swept AND reached", not strictly "reached after
            // sweeping" — see the header note.
            int m = array.size(hBuf)
            if m >= 2
                if sh
                    [t1a, _o1, t2a, _q1, up1] = f_tgts(hBuf, lBuf, m - 2, ph, pl, true, cont)
                    if not na(t1a)
                        swHiT += 1
                        if up1 ? h >= t1a : l <= t1a
                            tgHi += 1
                    if not na(t2a)
                        sw2HiT += 1
                        if up1 ? h >= t2a : l <= t2a
                            tg2Hi += 1
                if sl
                    [t1b, _o2, t2b, _q2, up2] = f_tgts(hBuf, lBuf, m - 2, ph, pl, false, cont)
                    if not na(t1b)
                        swLoT += 1
                        if up2 ? h >= t1b : l <= t1b
                            tgLo += 1
                    if not na(t2b)
                        sw2LoT += 1
                        if up2 ? h >= t2b : l <= t2b
                            tg2Lo += 1

            array.push(recHi, sh ? 1.0 : 0.0)
            array.push(recLo, sl ? 1.0 : 0.0)
            if array.size(recHi) > recN
                array.shift(recHi)
                array.shift(recLo)

    // Extend the buffer with the period that just completed. Kept outside the
    // scoring guard so the buffer stays dense and its last entry is always the
    // most recent completed period.
    if bar_index > 0 and not na(high[1]) and not na(low[1])
        array.push(hBuf, high[1])
        array.push(lBuf, low[1])
        if array.size(hBuf) > look + 4
            array.shift(hBuf)
            array.shift(lBuf)

    // Live targets for the period now forming. The buffer's last entry is now
    // period [1] — the candle whose high and low are the marked levels — so it
    // is both the reference and the start of the search one step earlier.
    int mm = array.size(hBuf)
    float refHi = mm > 0 ? array.get(hBuf, mm - 1) : na
    float refLo = mm > 0 ? array.get(lBuf, mm - 1) : na
    [tgtForHi, offForHi, tgt2ForHi, off2ForHi, _uh] = f_tgts(hBuf, lBuf, mm - 2, refHi, refLo, true,  cont)
    [tgtForLo, offForLo, tgt2ForLo, off2ForLo, _ul] = f_tgts(hBuf, lBuf, mm - 2, refHi, refLo, false, cont)

    int nRec = array.size(recHi)
    float pSwHiAll = nTot > 0 ? swHi * 1.0 / nTot : na
    float pSwLoAll = nTot > 0 ? swLo * 1.0 / nTot : na
    float pRvHi    = swHi > 0 ? rvHi * 1.0 / swHi : na
    float pRvLo    = swLo > 0 ? rvLo * 1.0 / swLo : na
    float pSwHiRec = nRec > 0 ? array.avg(recHi) : na
    float pSwLoRec = nRec > 0 ? array.avg(recLo) : na
    float pTgHi    = swHiT > 0 ? tgHi * 1.0 / swHiT : na
    float pTgLo    = swLoT > 0 ? tgLo * 1.0 / swLoT : na
    float pTg2Hi   = sw2HiT > 0 ? tg2Hi * 1.0 / sw2HiT : na
    float pTg2Lo   = sw2LoT > 0 ? tg2Lo * 1.0 / sw2LoT : na

    // A tuple of plain numbers crosses the security boundary cheaply and is
    // na-safe: a symbol with no data at this bar yields na elements rather
    // than an undefined object.
    // tgtForHi / tgtForLo are the live Target 1 prices for a high / low sweep,
    // with how many periods back each was found so the line can be anchored.
    [high[1], low[1], pSwHiAll, pSwLoAll, pRvHi, pRvLo, pSwHiRec, pSwLoRec, nTot, nRec,
     tgtForHi, tgtForLo, pTgHi, pTgLo, swHiT, swLoT, offForHi, offForLo,
     tgt2ForHi, tgt2ForLo, pTg2Hi, pTg2Lo, sw2HiT, sw2LoT, off2ForHi, off2ForLo]

// Which way a target points is fixed by the mode: a high sweep aims up when
// continuing, a low sweep aims up when reversing.
contMode = tgtMode == "Continuation (same side)"
upHi = contMode
upLo = not contMode

// lookahead_on paired with strictly historical references ([1], [2], [3] inside
// the engine) is the correct idiom for previous-period levels. Without it the
// value delivered during a live period comes from the last CLOSED higher
// timeframe bar, so high[1] inside would resolve two periods back and every
// level would be off by one. Because nothing here ever reads the forming bar,
// lookahead leaks no future data.
[dHi, dLo, dSwH, dSwL, dRvH, dRvL, dRcH, dRcL, dN, dNr, dTgH, dTgL, dPtH, dPtL, dTnH, dTnL, dOfH, dOfL, dT2H, dT2L, dP2H, dP2L, dN2H, dN2L, dO2H, dO2L] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "1D",  f_liq(recentN, tgtLook, contMode), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[wHi, wLo, wSwH, wSwL, wRvH, wRvL, wRcH, wRcL, wN, wNr, wTgH, wTgL, wPtH, wPtL, wTnH, wTnL, wOfH, wOfL, wT2H, wT2L, wP2H, wP2L, wN2H, wN2L, wO2H, wO2L] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "1W",  f_liq(recentN, tgtLook, contMode), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[mHi, mLo, mSwH, mSwL, mRvH, mRvL, mRcH, mRcL, mN, mNr, mTgH, mTgL, mPtH, mPtL, mTnH, mTnL, mOfH, mOfL, mT2H, mT2L, mP2H, mP2L, mN2H, mN2L, mO2H, mO2L] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "1M",  f_liq(recentN, tgtLook, contMode), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[yHi, yLo, ySwH, ySwL, yRvH, yRvL, yRcH, yRcL, yN, yNr, yTgH, yTgL, yPtH, yPtL, yTnH, yTnL, yOfH, yOfL, yT2H, yT2L, yP2H, yP2L, yN2H, yN2L, yO2H, yO2L] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "12M", f_liq(recentN, tgtLook, contMode), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

// ====================== Chart-side period tracking ===========================
// Index 0 = Day, 1 = Week, 2 = Month, 3 = Year.
// A target can be found any number of periods back, so instead of a fixed set
// of anchors each timeframe keeps a rolling list of period start bars. Offset
// 0 is the period now forming, 1 the period that supplied the levels, and so
// on, which lets any line be anchored to the exact candle it came from.
type PBuf
    array<int> starts

var array<PBuf> pb      = array.new<PBuf>()
var array<bool> hitHi   = array.new<bool>(4, false)
var array<bool> hitLo   = array.new<bool>(4, false)
var array<bool> tgtHiOk = array.new<bool>(4, false)
var array<bool> tgtLoOk = array.new<bool>(4, false)
var array<bool> tg2HiOk = array.new<bool>(4, false)
var array<bool> tg2LoOk = array.new<bool>(4, false)

if array.size(pb) == 0
    for i = 0 to 3
        array.push(pb, PBuf.new(starts = array.new<int>()))

newD = ta.change(time("1D"))  != 0
newW = ta.change(time("1W"))  != 0
newM = ta.change(time("1M"))  != 0
newY = ta.change(time("12M")) != 0

f_roll(int i, bool isNew) =>
    if isNew
        array<int> st = array.get(pb, i).starts
        array.push(st, bar_index)
        if array.size(st) > tgtLook + 6
            array.shift(st)
        array.set(hitHi,   i, false)
        array.set(hitLo,   i, false)
        array.set(tgtHiOk, i, false)
        array.set(tgtLoOk, i, false)
        array.set(tg2HiOk, i, false)
        array.set(tg2LoOk, i, false)
    isNew

// Start bar of the period `k` back from the one now forming.
f_startOf(int i, int k) =>
    array<int> st = array.get(pb, i).starts
    int m = array.size(st)
    int idx = m - 1 - k
    idx >= 0 and idx < m ? array.get(st, idx) : na

f_roll(0, newD)
f_roll(1, newW)
f_roll(2, newM)
f_roll(3, newY)

// ---- live sweep detection: has this level already been taken this period? ---
f_mark(int i, float lvlHi, float lvlLo) =>
    bool firedHi = false
    bool firedLo = false
    if not na(lvlHi) and high > lvlHi and not array.get(hitHi, i)
        array.set(hitHi, i, true)
        firedHi := true
    if not na(lvlLo) and low < lvlLo and not array.get(hitLo, i)
        array.set(hitLo, i, true)
        firedLo := true
    [firedHi, firedLo]

[fdH, fdL] = f_mark(0, dHi, dLo)
[fwH, fwL] = f_mark(1, wHi, wLo)
[fmH, fmL] = f_mark(2, mHi, mLo)
[fyH, fyL] = f_mark(3, yHi, yLo)

// ---- live target detection, strictly after its level was taken --------------
// A high sweep aims DOWN at tHi (the low two periods back); a low sweep aims UP
// at tLo (the high two periods back).
// T2 sits beyond T1 on the same side, so reaching it implies T1 was passed on
// the way; no extra ordering logic is needed beyond requiring the sweep first.
f_target(int i, float tHi, float tLo, float t2Hi, float t2Lo) =>
    bool firedHi = false
    bool firedLo = false
    bool fired2Hi = false
    bool fired2Lo = false
    if array.get(hitHi, i) and not na(tHi) and (upHi ? high >= tHi : low <= tHi) and not array.get(tgtHiOk, i)
        array.set(tgtHiOk, i, true)
        firedHi := true
    if array.get(hitLo, i) and not na(tLo) and (upLo ? high >= tLo : low <= tLo) and not array.get(tgtLoOk, i)
        array.set(tgtLoOk, i, true)
        firedLo := true
    if array.get(hitHi, i) and not na(t2Hi) and (upHi ? high >= t2Hi : low <= t2Hi) and not array.get(tg2HiOk, i)
        array.set(tg2HiOk, i, true)
        fired2Hi := true
    if array.get(hitLo, i) and not na(t2Lo) and (upLo ? high >= t2Lo : low <= t2Lo) and not array.get(tg2LoOk, i)
        array.set(tg2LoOk, i, true)
        fired2Lo := true
    [firedHi, firedLo, fired2Hi, fired2Lo]

[tdH, tdL, udH, udL] = f_target(0, dTgH, dTgL, dT2H, dT2L)
[twH, twL, uwH, uwL] = f_target(1, wTgH, wTgL, wT2H, wT2L)
[tmH, tmL, umH, umL] = f_target(2, mTgH, mTgL, mT2H, mT2L)
[tyH, tyL, uyH, uyL] = f_target(3, yTgH, yTgL, yT2H, yT2L)

// ================================ Drawing ====================================
var array<line>  lns = array.new<line>()
var array<label> lbs = array.new<label>()
var array<box>   bxs = array.new<box>()

f_style(string s) => s == "Dashed" ? line.style_dashed : s == "Dotted" ? line.style_dotted : line.style_solid
styleSel = f_style(lineSty)
tgtStyle = f_style(tgtSty)
lblSzSel = lblSize == "tiny" ? size.tiny : lblSize == "normal" ? size.normal : size.small

f_pct(float p) => na(p) ? "—" : str.tostring(math.round(p * 100)) + "%"

// One level: line anchored at its source candle, plus a price label.
f_level(int i, string tag, color col, float lvl, float pSweep, float n, bool swept) =>
    if not na(lvl) and not (hideSwept and swept)
        int src = f_startOf(i, 1)
        int x1 = na(src) ? math.max(0, bar_index - 100) : src
        color c = swept ? sweptCol : col
        line ln = line.new(x1, lvl, bar_index + rightPad, lvl, xloc=xloc.bar_index,
             color=c, style=swept ? line.style_dotted : styleSel, width=lineW)
        array.push(lns, ln)
        string txt = tag + "  " + str.tostring(lvl, format.mintick)
        if probIn
            txt += "  " + f_pct(pSweep)
        if swept
            txt += "  SWEPT"
        label lb = label.new(bar_index + rightPad, lvl, txt, xloc=xloc.bar_index,
             style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(c, 88), textcolor=c,
             size=lblSzSel, tooltip="Sample: " + str.tostring(n, "#") + " periods" + (nz(n) < minN ? "  (thin)" : ""))
        array.push(lbs, lb)
    true

// Target 1: anchored at the period two back that produced it. Drawn only once
// its level has been swept, unless the user asks to see targets in advance.
f_target1(int i, string tag, color tfCol, float lvl, float p, float n, int off, bool active, bool reached, bool rung2) =>
    if (rung2 ? showTgt2 : showTgt) and not na(lvl) and (active or tgtAlways)
        int src = f_startOf(i, off)
        int x1 = na(src) ? math.max(0, bar_index - 100) : src
        color baseC = tgtByTf ? tfCol : tgtCol
        color c = reached ? sweptCol : active ? baseC : color.new(baseC, 55)
        line ln = line.new(x1, lvl, bar_index + rightPad, lvl, xloc=xloc.bar_index,
             color=rung2 ? color.new(c, 35) : c, style=reached ? line.style_dotted : tgtStyle, width=tgtW)
        array.push(lns, ln)
        string txt = tag + "  " + str.tostring(lvl, format.mintick)
        if probIn
            txt += "  " + f_pct(p)
        txt += reached ? "  HIT" : active ? "  LIVE" : "  pending"
        label lb = label.new(bar_index + rightPad, lvl, txt, xloc=xloc.bar_index,
             style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(c, 88), textcolor=c,
             size=lblSzSel, tooltip="Target 1 for " + tag + ": reached on " + f_pct(p) + " of the " +
                  str.tostring(n, "#") + " recorded sweeps of this level.\nFound " +
                  str.tostring(off) + " periods back — the nearest candle extending beyond the swept one.\nMode: " + tgtMode)
        array.push(lbs, lb)
    true

// Shade the period the levels came from, so the source candle is unmistakable.
f_srcBox(int i, color col, float hi, float lo) =>
    int sx = f_startOf(i, 1)
    if showBox and not na(hi) and not na(lo) and not na(sx)
        int x1 = sx
        int cx = f_startOf(i, 0)
        int x2 = na(cx) ? bar_index : cx
        if x2 > x1
            array.push(bxs, box.new(x1, hi, x2, lo, xloc=xloc.bar_index,
                 border_color=color.new(col, 70), bgcolor=color.new(col, 93)))
    true

if barstate.islast
    for l in lns
        line.delete(l)
    array.clear(lns)
    for lb in lbs
        label.delete(lb)
    array.clear(lbs)
    for b in bxs
        box.delete(b)
    array.clear(bxs)

    if onD
        f_srcBox(0, colD, dHi, dLo)
        if showHi
            f_level(0, "PDH", colD, dHi, dSwH, dN, array.get(hitHi, 0))
            f_target1(0, "PDH T1", colD, dTgH, dPtH, dTnH, dOfH, array.get(hitHi, 0), array.get(tgtHiOk, 0), false)
            f_target1(0, "PDH T2", colD, dT2H, dP2H, dN2H, dO2H, array.get(hitHi, 0), array.get(tg2HiOk, 0), true)
        if showLo
            f_level(0, "PDL", colD, dLo, dSwL, dN, array.get(hitLo, 0))
            f_target1(0, "PDL T1", colD, dTgL, dPtL, dTnL, dOfL, array.get(hitLo, 0), array.get(tgtLoOk, 0), false)
            f_target1(0, "PDL T2", colD, dT2L, dP2L, dN2L, dO2L, array.get(hitLo, 0), array.get(tg2LoOk, 0), true)
    if onW
        f_srcBox(1, colW, wHi, wLo)
        if showHi
            f_level(1, "PWH", colW, wHi, wSwH, wN, array.get(hitHi, 1))
            f_target1(1, "PWH T1", colW, wTgH, wPtH, wTnH, wOfH, array.get(hitHi, 1), array.get(tgtHiOk, 1), false)
            f_target1(1, "PWH T2", colW, wT2H, wP2H, wN2H, wO2H, array.get(hitHi, 1), array.get(tg2HiOk, 1), true)
        if showLo
            f_level(1, "PWL", colW, wLo, wSwL, wN, array.get(hitLo, 1))
            f_target1(1, "PWL T1", colW, wTgL, wPtL, wTnL, wOfL, array.get(hitLo, 1), array.get(tgtLoOk, 1), false)
            f_target1(1, "PWL T2", colW, wT2L, wP2L, wN2L, wO2L, array.get(hitLo, 1), array.get(tg2LoOk, 1), true)
    if onM
        f_srcBox(2, colM, mHi, mLo)
        if showHi
            f_level(2, "PMH", colM, mHi, mSwH, mN, array.get(hitHi, 2))
            f_target1(2, "PMH T1", colM, mTgH, mPtH, mTnH, mOfH, array.get(hitHi, 2), array.get(tgtHiOk, 2), false)
            f_target1(2, "PMH T2", colM, mT2H, mP2H, mN2H, mO2H, array.get(hitHi, 2), array.get(tg2HiOk, 2), true)
        if showLo
            f_level(2, "PML", colM, mLo, mSwL, mN, array.get(hitLo, 2))
            f_target1(2, "PML T1", colM, mTgL, mPtL, mTnL, mOfL, array.get(hitLo, 2), array.get(tgtLoOk, 2), false)
            f_target1(2, "PML T2", colM, mT2L, mP2L, mN2L, mO2L, array.get(hitLo, 2), array.get(tg2LoOk, 2), true)
    if onY
        f_srcBox(3, colY, yHi, yLo)
        if showHi
            f_level(3, "PYH", colY, yHi, ySwH, yN, array.get(hitHi, 3))
            f_target1(3, "PYH T1", colY, yTgH, yPtH, yTnH, yOfH, array.get(hitHi, 3), array.get(tgtHiOk, 3), false)
            f_target1(3, "PYH T2", colY, yT2H, yP2H, yN2H, yO2H, array.get(hitHi, 3), array.get(tg2HiOk, 3), true)
        if showLo
            f_level(3, "PYL", colY, yLo, ySwL, yN, array.get(hitLo, 3))
            f_target1(3, "PYL T1", colY, yTgL, yPtL, yTnL, yOfL, array.get(hitLo, 3), array.get(tgtLoOk, 3), false)
            f_target1(3, "PYL T2", colY, yT2L, yP2L, yN2L, yO2L, array.get(hitLo, 3), array.get(tg2LoOk, 3), true)

// ================================= Alerts ====================================
anyHi  = fdH or fwH or fmH or fyH
anyLo  = fdL or fwL or fmL or fyL
anyTgt  = tdH or tdL or twH or twL or tmH or tmL or tyH or tyL
anyTgt2 = udH or udL or uwH or uwL or umH or umL or uyH or uyL

alertcondition(anyHi,  "Buy-side liquidity swept",  "A previous high was taken")
alertcondition(anyLo,  "Sell-side liquidity swept", "A previous low was taken")
alertcondition(anyTgt,  "Target 1 reached",         "Price reached Target 1 after a sweep")
alertcondition(anyTgt2, "Target 2 reached",         "Price reached Target 2 after a sweep")

f_alert(bool fired, string tag, float lvl, float p) =>
    if alertOn and fired
        alert(syminfo.ticker + "  " + tag + " swept at " + str.tostring(lvl, format.mintick) +
             "  (historical sweep rate " + f_pct(p) + ")", alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    fired

f_alertT(bool fired, string tag, string rung, float lvl, float p) =>
    if alertOn and fired
        alert(syminfo.ticker + "  " + tag + " " + rung + " reached at " + str.tostring(lvl, format.mintick) +
             "  (historical hit rate " + f_pct(p) + ")", alert.freq_once_per_bar)
    fired

f_alert(fdH, "PDH", dHi, dSwH)
f_alert(fdL, "PDL", dLo, dSwL)
f_alert(fwH, "PWH", wHi, wSwH)
f_alert(fwL, "PWL", wLo, wSwL)
f_alert(fmH, "PMH", mHi, mSwH)
f_alert(fmL, "PML", mLo, mSwL)
f_alert(fyH, "PYH", yHi, ySwH)
f_alert(fyL, "PYL", yLo, ySwL)

f_alertT(tdH, "PDH", "Target 1", dTgH, dPtH)
f_alertT(udH, "PDH", "Target 2", dT2H, dP2H)
f_alertT(tdL, "PDL", "Target 1", dTgL, dPtL)
f_alertT(udL, "PDL", "Target 2", dT2L, dP2L)
f_alertT(twH, "PWH", "Target 1", wTgH, wPtH)
f_alertT(uwH, "PWH", "Target 2", wT2H, wP2H)
f_alertT(twL, "PWL", "Target 1", wTgL, wPtL)
f_alertT(uwL, "PWL", "Target 2", wT2L, wP2L)
f_alertT(tmH, "PMH", "Target 1", mTgH, mPtH)
f_alertT(umH, "PMH", "Target 2", mT2H, mP2H)
f_alertT(tmL, "PML", "Target 1", mTgL, mPtL)
f_alertT(umL, "PML", "Target 2", mT2L, mP2L)
f_alertT(tyH, "PYH", "Target 1", yTgH, yPtH)
f_alertT(uyH, "PYH", "Target 2", yT2H, yP2H)
f_alertT(tyL, "PYL", "Target 1", yTgL, yPtL)
f_alertT(uyL, "PYL", "Target 2", yT2L, yP2L)

// =============================== Stats table =================================
posSel  = tblPos == "top_left" ? position.top_left : tblPos == "bottom_right" ? position.bottom_right : tblPos == "bottom_left" ? position.bottom_left : tblPos == "middle_right" ? position.middle_right : position.top_right
tSzSel  = tblSize == "tiny" ? size.tiny : tblSize == "normal" ? size.normal : tblSize == "large" ? size.large : size.small

var table t = table.new(posSel, 11, 10, border_width=1, frame_color=color.new(color.gray, 55), frame_width=1)

f_row(int r, string tag, color col, float lvl, float pAll, float pRec, float pRev,
      float tgt, float pTgt, float tgt2, float pTgt2, float n, bool swept, bool tgtDone, bool tgt2Done) =>
    bg   = color.new(color.black, 15)
    warn = color.new(color.orange, 40)
    cellBg = nz(n) < minN ? warn : bg
    table.cell(t, 0, r, tag, bgcolor=bg, text_color=col, text_size=tSzSel)
    table.cell(t, 1, r, na(lvl) ? "—" : str.tostring(lvl, format.mintick), bgcolor=bg, text_color=color.white, text_size=tSzSel)
    table.cell(t, 2, r, f_pct(pAll), bgcolor=cellBg, text_color=color.white, text_size=tSzSel)
    table.cell(t, 3, r, f_pct(pRec), bgcolor=cellBg, text_color=color.white, text_size=tSzSel)
    table.cell(t, 4, r, f_pct(pRev), bgcolor=cellBg, text_color=color.white, text_size=tSzSel)
    string noneTip = "No earlier candle within the search depth (" + str.tostring(tgtLook) + " periods) extends beyond the swept one, so there is no target to draw.\n\nIn continuation mode an upside target needs an earlier candle with a HIGHER high. At or near new highs none exists nearby — common on crypto. Raise the target search depth, or switch to Reversal mode."
    table.cell(t, 5, r, na(tgt) ? "none" : str.tostring(tgt, format.mintick), bgcolor=bg, text_color=na(tgt) ? color.gray : tgtDone ? color.gray : (tgtByTf ? col : tgtCol), text_size=tSzSel, tooltip=na(tgt) ? noneTip : "Target 1. A price here but no line on the chart means the level has not been swept yet — turn on \"Show targets before the sweep\" to see it in advance.")
    table.cell(t, 6, r, f_pct(pTgt), bgcolor=cellBg, text_color=color.white, text_size=tSzSel)
    table.cell(t, 7, r, na(tgt2) ? "none" : str.tostring(tgt2, format.mintick), bgcolor=bg, text_color=na(tgt2) ? color.gray : tgt2Done ? color.gray : (tgtByTf ? col : tgtCol), text_size=tSzSel, tooltip=na(tgt2) ? noneTip : "Target 2, the next rung beyond Target 1.")
    table.cell(t, 8, r, f_pct(pTgt2), bgcolor=cellBg, text_color=color.white, text_size=tSzSel)
    table.cell(t, 9, r, str.tostring(n, "#"), bgcolor=bg, text_color=color.gray, text_size=tSzSel)
    table.cell(t, 10, r, tgt2Done ? "T2 HIT" : tgtDone ? "T1 HIT" : swept ? "SWEPT" : "open", bgcolor=bg,
         text_color=(tgtDone or tgt2Done) ? (tgtByTf ? col : tgtCol) : swept ? color.gray : col, text_size=tSzSel)
    true

if barstate.islast and showTbl
    hbg = color.new(color.gray, 35)
    table.cell(t, 0, 0, "Level",  bgcolor=hbg, text_color=color.white, text_size=tSzSel)
    table.cell(t, 1, 0, "Price",  bgcolor=hbg, text_color=color.white, text_size=tSzSel)
    table.cell(t, 2, 0, "Sweep",  bgcolor=hbg, text_color=color.white, text_size=tSzSel, tooltip="Share of periods in which this level was traded through at some point. All available history.")
    table.cell(t, 3, 0, "Recent", bgcolor=hbg, text_color=color.white, text_size=tSzSel, tooltip="Same probability over the last " + str.tostring(recentN) + " periods only. A wide gap versus the all-time column means behaviour has shifted.")
    table.cell(t, 4, 0, "Rev",    bgcolor=hbg, text_color=color.white, text_size=tSzSel, tooltip="Of the times this level was swept, how often price closed back inside it. High = stop hunt and reversal. Low = the level breaks and price keeps going.")
    table.cell(t, 5, 0, "T1",     bgcolor=hbg, text_color=color.white, text_size=tSzSel, tooltip="Target 1 under the current mode (" + tgtMode + "): the nearest earlier candle that extends beyond the one that supplied this level, searched from two periods back.")
    table.cell(t, 6, 0, "T1 hit", bgcolor=hbg, text_color=color.white, text_size=tSzSel, tooltip="Given this level was swept, how often price also reached Target 1 in the same period. A single higher-timeframe candle does not record whether the high came before the low, so this counts 'swept AND reached' rather than strictly 'reached after sweeping'.")
    table.cell(t, 7, 0, "T2",     bgcolor=hbg, text_color=color.white, text_size=tSzSel, tooltip="Target 2: the first candle beyond Target 1 in the same direction — the next pool of liquidity out.")
    table.cell(t, 8, 0, "T2 hit", bgcolor=hbg, text_color=color.white, text_size=tSzSel, tooltip="Given this level was swept, how often price also reached Target 2. Always at or below the T1 figure, since T2 lies beyond T1 on the same side. The gap between the two columns is how often a move that reaches T1 keeps going.")
    table.cell(t, 9, 0, "n",      bgcolor=hbg, text_color=color.white, text_size=tSzSel)
    table.cell(t, 10, 0, "Status", bgcolor=hbg, text_color=color.white, text_size=tSzSel)

    int r = 1
    if onD and showHi
        f_row(r, "PDH", colD, dHi, dSwH, dRcH, dRvH, dTgH, dPtH, dT2H, dP2H, dN, array.get(hitHi, 0), array.get(tgtHiOk, 0), array.get(tg2HiOk, 0))
        r += 1
    if onD and showLo
        f_row(r, "PDL", colD, dLo, dSwL, dRcL, dRvL, dTgL, dPtL, dT2L, dP2L, dN, array.get(hitLo, 0), array.get(tgtLoOk, 0), array.get(tg2LoOk, 0))
        r += 1
    if onW and showHi
        f_row(r, "PWH", colW, wHi, wSwH, wRcH, wRvH, wTgH, wPtH, wT2H, wP2H, wN, array.get(hitHi, 1), array.get(tgtHiOk, 1), array.get(tg2HiOk, 1))
        r += 1
    if onW and showLo
        f_row(r, "PWL", colW, wLo, wSwL, wRcL, wRvL, wTgL, wPtL, wT2L, wP2L, wN, array.get(hitLo, 1), array.get(tgtLoOk, 1), array.get(tg2LoOk, 1))
        r += 1
    if onM and showHi
        f_row(r, "PMH", colM, mHi, mSwH, mRcH, mRvH, mTgH, mPtH, mT2H, mP2H, mN, array.get(hitHi, 2), array.get(tgtHiOk, 2), array.get(tg2HiOk, 2))
        r += 1
    if onM and showLo
        f_row(r, "PML", colM, mLo, mSwL, mRcL, mRvL, mTgL, mPtL, mT2L, mP2L, mN, array.get(hitLo, 2), array.get(tgtLoOk, 2), array.get(tg2LoOk, 2))
        r += 1
    if onY and showHi
        f_row(r, "PYH", colY, yHi, ySwH, yRcH, yRvH, yTgH, yPtH, yT2H, yP2H, yN, array.get(hitHi, 3), array.get(tgtHiOk, 3), array.get(tg2HiOk, 3))
        r += 1
    if onY and showLo
        f_row(r, "PYL", colY, yLo, ySwL, yRcL, yRvL, yTgL, yPtL, yT2L, yP2L, yN, array.get(hitLo, 3), array.get(tgtLoOk, 3), array.get(tg2LoOk, 3))
        r += 1
